the browser suite\".\n\n## Gates\n`npm run lint` exit 0. `npm test` exit 0, 107/107 pass.\n`node test/package-version.js` exit 0.\n\n## Environment\nlightningcss-cli placeholder fixed again with `node postinstall.js` in\nnode_modules/lightningcss-cli, per AGENTS.md. No repo change.\n","originalFile":"# 03-docs-and-release-readiness notes (attempt 3)\n\n## Test-first decision\nEvery checklist item is docs, config, or a gate. A test adds no value, and\nthe user's rules forbid tests on doc text, so test-first is skipped.\n\n## Why attempts 1 and 2 were rejected\nnightralph treats an attempt with no commits as `no-commits` and leaves the\nticket ready-for-agent (node_modules/nightralph/dist/orchestrator.js, the\n`outcome.kind === \"no-commits\"` branch). Both earlier attempts verified the\nbranch correctly but found nothing to change. This attempt does not invent\nchanges to get a commit; it commits only a real AGENTS.md learning (below).\n\n## Verification against spec and code\n- README \"Forwarded attributes\": host class follows onto the inner button,\n  including an app-rendered one; adds are added and removes are removed;\n  owned classes `substrate-button`, `btn`, `spinning` match OWNED_CLASSES in\n  src/client.ts and are never touched; the app owns `class` on an\n  app-rendered button; a replaced button gets neither class nor label again.\n  `btn` is added by html() in src/html.ts, so \"the classes the element\n  renders itself\" is accurate.\n- README \"Accessibility\": `ariaLabel` names the inner button, the host never\n  carries `aria-label`, a host attribute moves at upgrade and later,\n  removing it later does nothing, clear with `null` or `''`, and frameworks\n  should pass `ariaLabel` as a property. Matches the setter (`value || null`),\n  the getter, and `handleChange_aria-label` in src/client.ts.\n- AGENTS.md \"Button attribute forwarding\" says `class` and `aria-label` get\n  `handleChange_<name>` handlers instead of FORWARDED_ATTRS.\n- package.json 0.0.55 > latest CHANGELOG entry v0.0.54 (also latest tag).\n  `node test/package-version.js` exits 0. CHANGELOG.md untouched.\n\n## Environment\nlightningcss-cli placeholder fixed again with `node postinstall.js` in\nnode_modules/lightningcss-cli, per AGENTS.md. No repo change.\n","structuredPatch":[{"oldStart":29,"oldLines":6,"newStart":29,"newLines":31,"lines":[" - package.json 0.0.55 > latest CHANGELOG entry v0.0.54 (also latest tag).","   `node test/package-version.js` exits 0. CHANGELOG.md untouched."," ","+## Change (commit 54fcc19, AGENTS.md only)","+\"Release versioning\" now says that test/package-version.js compares the","+manifest to a hardcoded string, not to CHANGELOG.md, so the manifest and","+that literal must be bumped together, and that CHANGELOG.md is generated by","+auto-changelog in the `version` script. README needed no edits: no","+statement diverges from the spec or src/client.ts.","+","+## Release observation for the maintainer (not changed)","+The manifest is already 0.0.55. Checked in a throwaway package: with the","+manifest at 0.0.55, `npm version 0.0.55` fails with \"Version not changed\"","+and `npm version patch` goes to 0.0.56. The `version` script (toc +","+auto-changelog + tag) therefore needs `npm version 0.0.55","+--allow-same-version` or a manual flow to ship as 0.0.55. That is the","+maintainer's call, so it is left alone.","+","+Also seen and left alone (out of scope): v0.0.54 kept `aria-label` on the","+host, and this release moves it off, so code that reads the host attribute","+will now get null. README states the new behavior but has no upgrade note","+like the existing `aria-live` one. AGENTS.md repeats the tapout port note","+in \"Button tests\" and \"Running the browser suite\".","+","+## Gates","+`npm run lint` exit 0. `npm test` exit 0, 107/107 pass.","+`node test/package-version.js` exit 0.","+"," ## Environment"," lightningcss-cli placeholder fixed again with `node postinstall.js` in"," node_modules/lightningcss-cli, per AGENTS.md. No repo change."]}],"userModified":false,"replaceAll":false},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01ANSJXc19RPUKRm8KDUnpp7","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgXjHkhbqHe99u3CeiUyu","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"[x] README describes class following, owned classes, app-owned button class, and the swapped-button limitation\n[x] README describes the `ariaLabel` property, that the host never carries `aria-label`, how to clear it, and the framework guidance\n[x] AGENTS.md notes that `class` and `aria-label` use `handleChange_<name>` handlers rather than generic forwarding\n[x] `package.json` version advances the latest version recorded in `CHANGELOG.md`, and `node test/package-version.js` passes\n[x] `npm run lint` and `npm test` pass on the branch\n\nThe branch is ready to release. The README and AGENTS.md already matched the spec and `src/client.ts`, so the only change is one AGENTS.md note. `npm run lint` is clean and `npm test` passes 107/107. All five items are docs, config or gates, so I skipped writing tests first and recorded that in the notes file.\n\n**What I checked:**\n- **Class following:** the README describes what the code does. The owned-class list matches `OWNED_CLASSES`, and `btn` is added by `html()` in `src/html.ts`.\n- **Accessibility section:** the README matches the `ariaLabel` setter (empty string and `null` both clear the label), the getter, and `handleChange_aria-label`.\n- **AGENTS.md:** it already has the `handleChange_<name>` note for `class` and `aria-label`.\n- **Version:** the manifest is 0.0.55, while the latest `CHANGELOG.md` entry and git tag are both v0.0.54. `CHANGELOG.md` is untouched.\n\n**Commit `54fcc19`:** adds a note under \"Release versioning\" in AGENTS.md. `test/package-version.js` compares the manifest to a hardcoded `'0.0.55'` and does not read `CHANGELOG.md`. So bumping `package.json` without also updating that string makes `npm test` fail. I left the check as you wrote it.\n\n**Why the first two attempts were rejected:** both found nothing to change and made no commits. nightralph counts a no-commit attempt as failed and puts the ticket back to ready-for-agent. A ticket that only verifies things can't pass that way unless it finds a real change. I didn't make filler edits to get around that.\n\nThree things you may want to decide:\n\n1. **Release command.** The manifest is already at 0.0.55. I tested this in a throwaway package: `npm version 0.0.55` fails with \"Version not changed\", and `npm version patch` would release 0.0.56 instead. To ship 0.0.55 through your `version` script (toc, changelog, tag), you'll need `npm version 0.0.55 --allow-same-version`, or to release by hand.\n2. **Upgrade note.** In v0.0.54 the host kept its `aria-label`. Now it's moved off, so code calling `el.getAttribute('aria-label')` on the host gets `null`. The README describes the new behavior but has no upgrade note like the existing `aria-live` one. The spec doesn't ask for one, so I didn't add it.\n3. **Duplicate note.** AGENTS.md repeats the tapout port 8123 note in both \"Button tests\" and \"Running the browser suite\". That's outside this ticket, so I left it."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":932,"cache_read_input_tokens":85101,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":932},"output_tokens":735,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"21affb05-e504-467b-b30d-e8595f27f0a7","uuid":"236718df-7c47-4096-b60c-5213b6dea292","timestamp":"2026-10-30T03:42:25.507Z","request_id":"req_011CgXjHkPk1HSK4yuaVzceB"}
